  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cultivating Change in a Warming World</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Technology Development Trust (CTDT - Zimbabwe and the Oxfam Country Office were selected to become the &quot;Knowledge Hub&quot; for the &quot;Umbrella Framework Cultivating Change in a Warming World&quot; project for the period April 2024 - March 2028. CTDT and Oxfam will take the work on Farmer Field Schools to scale in two (Mudzi and Uzumba Maramba Pfungwe) of the five districts where the SDHS program was implemented. At least fifteen FFS from the SDHS programme will be consolidated in each of the two districts per year. These will act as learning and knowledge hubs where farmers&apos; especially women will be further trained to develop their skills on agro -ecology, facilitation skills, participatory plant breeding (PPB, PVS, PVD), seed production and marketing. Women -led FFS will create platforms for sharing successful practices, lessons learnt and innovations and take these to scale within and outside their communities. These Farmer Field Schools will coalesce into networks to facilitate the scaling up of the work on commercialization of local food plants.</narrative>
  </description>
